Well, my Valkyrie Alyson made it (hooray)!  First time, no less.  
-- Obligatory spoiler warning --



























Just like my girlfriend.  Anything to get spoiled.

Anyway, excellent polypoling results gave Alyson a good AC, and the
"donate to non-aligned priest, then kill him/her" technique got the
total AC down to -42.  Had speed boots, GDSM, SoR, helm of telepathy,
displacement, and (naturally) GoP with +7 Mjollnir and +6 Vorpal Blade.

Had no trouble with the Quest; having intrinsic teleport/control to block
level-jumping monsters is really handy.  Medusa was trivial, but she got
the small island, not the big one.  By the time she was to the castle
level, she found enough enchant armor scrolls to make it trivial.  The WoW
only had one charge, but she found another with 3.  *NEVER* found a scroll
of charging, but she ended up not using any wishes until the Astral
Planes.

Never having been there, she really didn't know exactly what to expect.
Tried polymorphing into a Xorn on the Earth plane, did no damage to
monsters and reverted.  Digging and fighting seemed to have better
results.  Air plane was trivial; just ran through it.  Fire [sic] plane
was a bitch!  With six archons attacking at once, and one AoLS later,
I consider ring of conflict a necessity for this level.  Grabbing a
cockatrice corpse didn't hurt, either.  The Astral plane was a piece
of cake, save the major demons.

Ascended with >200000 gold, stressed with a blessed bag of holding worth of
gems, 8237418 points.  Ended with 479HP and 185SP, st:25, dx:18, co:17(18),
In:12(14), wi:18, and ch:12(13).  Lost some stats dealing with Pestilence
and Death (didn't know about *these* in advance)  Good thing Alyson knew
the cure sickness spell, because she forgot the potions.

Minor bugs noticed along the way:

"You are blinded by the invisible Archon's radiance!" - same paradox as
the invisible floating eye (although I could be convinced an Archon
could be invisible and radiant at the same time).

While polymorphed into a couatl, I was swallowed by a fire vortex.
Rested to get some HP back, and then tried to hack my way out.  Received
the message "The fire vortex is being crushed."  This seems to be a neat
trick from the INSIDE.  Maybe "the fire vortex is being distended"
instead.

Finally, I couldn't seem to sacrifice items dropped on altars in the astral
plane.

Now, for quick comment and suggestion:

There seems to be a lot of discussion on how monsters get AoLS and WoD
and can use them; the WoD thread seems to be somewhat settled.  Perhaps,
though, if you had telepathy or high Int, you would receive "You feel
a threatening emptiness" or "Your heart beats very loudly" if a monster
was carrying one in the area.  Although since I usually get reflection
before telepathy this might be of limited use.

I didn't like much seeing a hobbit be resurrected by its AoLS, though.
Instead of #look and #pickpocket features, perhaps you should receive a
message like "The hobbit confidently swings his rubber mace" so that you
would know he had something special, like AoLS.  Getting it should not
be any easier than poly into nymph, after all it *is* an AoLS.

Anyway, I had great fun playing.  Now if I can only find an amulet of
change so Dr. Beverly Crusher the Healer won't be quite so confused...

